{{also|FELIX|Felix|Félix}}
==Latin==

===Etymology===
from {{etyl|itc-pro|la}} root ''*fe-'', equivalent of {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} *dhe(i)- "to suck, suckle, produce, yield"

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈfeː.liːks/|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-3rd-1E|fēlīx|felicis#Latin|fēlīcis}}

# [[happy]], [[lucky]], [[blessed]], [[fortunate]]
# [[fertile]], [[fruitful]]
# [[auspicious]], [[favorable]], of [[good]] [[omen]] or [[luck]]
# {{context|religion|archaic}} of the [[noble]] [[fruit]]s offered to the [[deity|deities]]

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-3rd-1E|felix|fēlīx|felic|fēlīc}}

* ''comparative'': '''[[felicior|fēlīcior]]''', ''superlative'': '''[[felicissimus|fēlīcissimus]]'''

